          "reasoning": "On app-01, a root shell running `sh ./run_mod.sh` (proc-d345bba067) launched `sh ./mod_sudoer.sh` (proc-cde358715c, script file-1fa529ef7d) from /home/ubuntu. That script ran `sudo echo evil_user ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (proc-8f783cab26 -> echo proc-5113b0fdb3), then `sudo echo root ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (proc-3956796274). Both commands build passwordless-sudo rules, which matches sudoers privilege-escalation and persistence tradecraft (T1548.003). The only network traffic was a local DNS lookup to 127.0.0.53. A search turned up no confirmed write to a sudoers file, but the commands are plainly malicious in intent, so /etc/sudoers and sudoers.d need to be checked and cleaned up.",
